electromagnetic-field-bianchi-identity-5.conceptual_definition:
The Bianchi identity for the electromagnetic field, denoted as $\partial_{[\mu} F_{
u\lambda]} \equiv 0$, is the statement that the cyclic sum of partial derivatives of the electromagnetic field strength tensor $F_{\mu
u}$ is identically zero. This is equivalent to the expanded form $\partial_\mu F_{
u\lambda} + \partial_
u F_{\lambda\mu} + \partial_\lambda F_{\mu
u} = 0$.

